/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 56 0 R
/T (Every number a mariner needs already exists. Wave height comes from one model, wind from another, satellite sea-surface temperature from a third, official warnings from a fourth, and maritime boundaries from a fifth. Each lives behind its own portal, its own file format and its own update clock. The work of reconciling them falls on the person least equipped to do it usually at four in the morning, on a phone, before deciding whether to put to sea.)
/E (Every number a mariner needs already exists. Wave height comes from one model, wind from another, satellite sea-surface temperature from a third, official warnings from a fourth, and maritime boundaries from a fifth. Each lives behind its own portal, its own file format and its own update clock. The work of reconciling them falls on the person least equipped to do it usually at four in the morning, on a phone, before deciding whether to put to sea.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [44]
>>
endobj
