/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
395 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 64 0 R
/E (Sources answer different questions and are treated differently. Open-Meteo answers a whole date span in one request, so ninety days of wave height is one call; ERDDAP griddap answers one timestamp, so ninety days of MUR SST is ninety calls. A twenty-day, thirteen-variable build costs 22 upstream requests rather than 260, and the request is costed and refused with the figure before it runs rather than dying at a proxy timeout.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
396 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 64 0 R
/T (11.  Provenance, and the refusal to guess)
/E (11.  Provenance, and the refusal to guess)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
397 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 64 0 R
/E (Nothing reaches the user as a bare number. Every value arrives wrapped in evidence naming its dataset, its age, and one of six provenance states LIVE, CACHED, CURATED, DERIVED, SIMULATED, UNAVAILABLE. A derived value must declare its lineage. An advisory with no citation fails validation at the type level, so an uncited answer is not a representable state.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
398 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 64 0 R
/E (What this looks like when things go wrong)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
399 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 64 0 R
/E (If the wind feed fails, ORCA does not fill the gap with a plausible number. It returns the verdict it can defend, marks the missing inputs UNVERIFIABLE, lowers its confidence, and tells the user to confirm with their fisheries office or the coastal VHF channel before sailing. A system that is confidently wrong at sea is worse than one that admits the gap.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
400 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 64 0 R
/E (The same discipline governs what we chose not to build. Storm-surge modelling needs validated bathymetry and expert calibration, so it is absent rather than approximated. Live cyclone tracking is not derived from a best-track archive, because presenting hindsight as a live warning during a cyclone is the worst thing this system could do.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
