432 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 65 0 R
/E (The frontend is served from a global edge network; the API runs on a dedicated-IP instance behind an automatically renewing TLS certificate, supervised so it survives reboots. The dedicated address matters for a specific reason: free-tier weather APIs count their quota per IP, and on shared hosting that quota is consumed by strangers, which produced rate-limit failures that looked like bugs in our own code.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [27]
>>
endobj
433 0 obj
<<
