1489 0 obj
<<
/Title (Every number a mariner needs already exists. Wave height comes from one model, wind from another, satellite sea-surface temperature from a third, official warnings from a fourth, and maritime boundaries from a fifth. Each lives behind its own portal, its own file format and its own update clock. The work of reconciling them falls on the person least equipped to do it usually at four in the morning, on a phone, before deciding whether to put to sea.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1407 0 R
/Next 1490 0 R
>>
endobj
1490 0 obj
<<
/Title (ORCA does that reconciliation. It is a reasoning layer, not another dashboard: you ask a question in your own language, and it plans which sources to consult, fetches them, cross-checks them, and answers with a verdict plus every number behind it.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1407 0 R
/Prev 1489 0 R
>>
